message: Please cite the paper; this repository supplies its source.
type: software
title: "Forgetting under noise is undecidable"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: '2026-11-12'
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24176024"
license: [CC-BY-4.0, MIT, Apache-2.0]
authors: [{"family-names": "Douglas", "given-names": "Seth", "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"}, {"family-names": "Mghirbi", "given-names": "Nidhal", "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6534-1118"}]
keywords: ["probabilistic cellular automata", "ergodicity", "undecidability", "positive rates", "Wang tiles", "Toom contours", "existential pebble games", "local consistency", "space-time Gibbs measures", "noise", "Gibbs measures", "weak spatial mixing", "Lean"]
abstract: "A natural noisy Wang rule on Z^4 is ergodic exactly when its finite raw tile set does not tile the plane. A cardinal checker and a fixed 512-of-768 quorum use the tiles themselves and one blank. A transverse-quorum lift of Kari's nilpotency reduction gives the same equivalence on Z^3 for north/east deterministic tile sets. One explicit positive rational replacement rate, independent of the input, makes ergodicity undecidable in both families. For non-tiling inputs, amortized coherence and an all-path density lemma prove finite-window coupling from the past for all starts; tiling gives two invariant laws. A saturation theorem explains why the earlier budget-only estimate needs six dimensions. The retained Z^6 natural rule has exponential all-input coalescence with a universal computable slope and uncomputable delay, all-Gibbs uniqueness and robustness. Its Theorems D and A are verified in Lean; the Z^4 and Z^3 results are not formalized. The inspector theory and Z^8 machine-family Lean core are retained."
